// Weapon shapes (melee-and-ranged 3.1: 18 shapes across materials). Volumes are real cm3 of material (steel 7.85 g/cm3: arming-sword
// blade 180 cm3 = 1.41 kg). Contact areas, penetration (mm) and velocity multipliers are DF-style estimates, calibrated with tools/calibrate
// against resolver-v2 section 8. Wind-up and recover for dagger, sword, axe, maul and spear are plan §4A.3; the rest are the melee spec's.
// v2 fields: family, reach_mm, strike_ticks (the 20 Hz timeline is P4-C); shield_cover_pm on an attack scales a shield's cover (flail 500).
// The maul's contact area is 25 (was 60, open question Q22: its blunt need, proportional to area, made it worse than a mace).
